WEBVTT

00:01.710 --> 00:03.850
Wh-What is this?!

00:03.850 --> 00:07.230
Those are the ingredients for
 today's home ec class!

00:07.230 --> 00:11.280
That I get, I think, but...

00:11.280 --> 00:14.390
But why are you hanging from 
the ceiling, Wiz-sensei?

00:14.390 --> 00:15.260
Well...

00:15.260 --> 00:20.590
Because this failure of a teacher bought 
too much of the wrong thing again!

00:20.590 --> 00:22.410
Vanir-sensei!

00:22.410 --> 00:29.170
Home ec classes should make simple 
things like curry and egg dishes!

00:29.170 --> 00:33.190
So where the hell did all this come from?

00:34.310 --> 00:38.900
I just thought pasta would be 
an easy dish for everyone.

00:38.900 --> 00:40.940
The problem is the amount you bought!

00:40.940 --> 00:45.090
And look at all these ingredients!
 They're impossible for beginners to prepare!

00:45.090 --> 00:46.660
They're all top-quality ingredients!

00:46.660 --> 00:48.060
That's not the issue!

00:48.440 --> 00:51.160
What a waste of money.

00:51.160 --> 00:55.470
But I paid for what the budget wouldn't 
cover out of my own pocket.

00:55.870 --> 00:56.890
Please!

00:56.890 --> 00:59.450
No Vanir-Style Murder Beams!

00:59.750 --> 01:02.390
It's fine, Wiz-sensei.

01:02.390 --> 01:05.460
Everyone's friends in this world.

01:05.460 --> 01:07.960
He can't fire murder beams...

01:07.960 --> 01:11.960
WIZ-SENSEI!

01:17.180 --> 01:24.800
ISEKAI QUARTET 3

02:38.550 --> 02:42.000
ISEKAI QUARTET 3

02:42.010 --> 02:45.010
- Episode 4: Chaos! Cooking Class!
- HOME ECONOMICS

02:42.860 --> 02:44.460
Sheesh...

02:45.010 --> 02:48.820
I never thought I'd end up 
drowning in pasta in this world, too.

02:48.820 --> 02:50.820
I agree completely.

02:50.820 --> 02:52.230
Also...

02:52.900 --> 02:56.230
Why is Wiz-sensei hanging from the ceiling?

02:57.300 --> 03:01.750
You, the little girl whose appearance and 
mind are nothing alike! And her servants!

03:02.100 --> 03:05.490
Get together so I can split you into groups!

03:05.990 --> 03:08.310
This'll be rough.

03:08.310 --> 03:11.010
Lady Rem, can I ask you to take the lead here?

03:11.010 --> 03:12.530
Leave it to me.

03:13.040 --> 03:15.860
I don't know if I can make something 
you'll enjoy, Miss Lalatina.

03:15.860 --> 03:17.030
Don't call me that!

03:17.030 --> 03:19.090
Pervert noble, then?

03:20.010 --> 03:22.110
I'll do the eating!

03:22.110 --> 03:23.650
Is that how it works?

03:23.650 --> 03:26.140
Of course not. Unless you're me.

03:26.140 --> 03:27.740
Let's do our best, Mare-kun.

03:26.140 --> 03:28.490
Can you cook, Emilia?

03:27.740 --> 03:29.610
Y-Yes, let's!

03:28.490 --> 03:31.660
Yes, Subaru tells me he loves my cooking.

03:31.660 --> 03:35.190
Can we really trust you?

03:35.190 --> 03:38.220
Just don't screw this up for everyone.

03:38.710 --> 03:40.540
That's my line!

03:40.540 --> 03:42.740
Koenig-san, let's do our best.

03:42.740 --> 03:43.580
Yeah.

03:44.660 --> 03:49.440
Okay, everyone, let's start 
by boiling the pasta.

03:49.440 --> 03:50.300
Wait.

03:51.750 --> 03:54.770
I hear something from inside the bag.

03:54.770 --> 03:56.700
Could it be insects?

03:56.700 --> 03:59.370
It's not insects.

04:01.330 --> 04:05.150
The pasta's so fresh that it's still alive!

04:05.150 --> 04:06.150
Hold it!

04:07.220 --> 04:10.530
This is pasta! Pasta isn't alive...

04:10.530 --> 04:11.710
Wait.

04:11.710 --> 04:16.500
They do say the fresher the ingredients, 
the better, which implies... but...

04:14.700 --> 04:17.530
She's overthinking it so much
 that it's broken her brain.

04:17.530 --> 04:20.340
Well, sometimes you cook things that alive.

04:20.340 --> 04:22.200
D-Do you?

04:22.200 --> 04:22.940
Yup.

04:22.940 --> 04:24.750
In our world, you can get yourself

04:24.750 --> 04:28.850
killed by letting your guard 
down around cabbage and lettuce.

04:28.850 --> 04:29.910
Hold it!

04:29.910 --> 04:33.710
Different worlds have different 
ideas about what's normal.

04:34.110 --> 04:38.770
In your world, are pasta and lettuce 
and cabbage l-like this, too?

04:38.770 --> 04:41.710
Nope. Veggies are veggies.

04:41.710 --> 04:45.940
Whew. Ains, in your world...

04:47.010 --> 04:48.140
Never mind.

04:48.140 --> 04:51.590
In their world, anything could be alive.

04:54.610 --> 04:55.450
There.

04:59.930 --> 05:03.530
Some people might feel guilty about this.

05:03.530 --> 05:06.890
The strong decide whether the weak live or die.

05:06.890 --> 05:08.440
That is a fundamental rule.

05:08.440 --> 05:13.710
Yes. Our job is to just make sure 
their lives are put to delicious use.

05:13.710 --> 05:16.940
I'm glad you're both so bold.

05:16.940 --> 05:20.540
Wow, the conversation's proceeding 
without me having to say a thing.

05:20.540 --> 05:22.080
Yup.

05:22.080 --> 05:24.450
Nuemann, who are you talking to?

05:24.450 --> 05:25.860
That group over there.

05:25.860 --> 05:28.300
They're a long ways away, aren't they?

05:29.590 --> 05:31.140
It's finished!

05:32.350 --> 05:36.350
I call it "Explosion Luxury Seafood Pasta!"

05:37.300 --> 05:40.860
Crazy... This looks crazy good!

05:40.860 --> 05:42.490
Is this edible?

05:42.490 --> 05:44.990
I supervised them, so it's fine.

05:44.990 --> 05:46.740
We finished ours, too.

05:47.370 --> 05:51.530
I call it Devil-Style Chicken Cream Pasta!

05:51.530 --> 05:55.660
No way! It's Goddess-Style Chicken Cream Pasta!

05:56.890 --> 05:59.060
You guys made two different dishes?

05:59.060 --> 06:03.460
Just one. They're just fighting 
over what to call it.

06:03.460 --> 06:05.070
Subaru!

06:05.070 --> 06:06.340
Oh, right.

06:07.140 --> 06:09.290
We made something basic.

06:09.290 --> 06:12.110
Japanese-style mayonnaise pasta!

06:12.110 --> 06:15.260
With three different types of fish eggs!

06:15.260 --> 06:18.890
That's the type of dish where you just throw in 
lots of yummy things but often turns out wrong!

06:19.500 --> 06:22.850
We just made something ordinary.

06:22.850 --> 06:26.820
Most "ordinary" pasta dishes don't have 
sea urchin roe and black truffles.

06:27.100 --> 06:30.510
Hey, Tanya, was I useful?

06:30.510 --> 06:34.100
Yes, you helped a lot by 
chilling the pasta for us.

06:34.100 --> 06:37.090
And you did the tasting 
since Shalltear couldn't.

06:37.090 --> 06:41.370
You were wrong to ask an undead 
like me to be the taste tester.

06:41.370 --> 06:43.350
Sorry. I assigned you to the wrong job.

06:43.350 --> 06:44.450
I'll remember that for next time.

06:45.330 --> 06:48.910
Kazuma, you've shown incredible skill.

06:48.910 --> 06:50.680
D-Did I?

06:50.680 --> 06:55.110
Indeed. Kazuma, it seems I underestimated you.

06:55.110 --> 06:56.660
Aw, I'm blushing!

06:56.660 --> 06:58.860
Come on. Let's eat!

06:58.860 --> 07:01.170
Right. Give me a plate. Now.

07:01.170 --> 07:03.990
You two should learn a lesson 
from Demiurge and Cocytus.

07:06.570 --> 07:10.270
Okay, it's finally time to dig in!

07:10.270 --> 07:12.860
Start by tasting your own dish.

07:12.860 --> 07:16.740
Then go around to the other 
groups' tables and try theirs!

07:16.740 --> 07:18.570
Now...

07:18.570 --> 07:21.030
Let's eat!

07:24.210 --> 07:29.470
After seeing the pasta squirm, 
it's kind of hard to eat it.

07:29.470 --> 07:33.660
It's fine. They're dead now, so they won't move.

07:33.660 --> 07:36.260
True, they're not... moving...

07:37.170 --> 07:37.970
Huh?

07:38.250 --> 07:40.220
Did it just move?

07:40.220 --> 07:43.350
Of course not. Don't be silly.

07:43.350 --> 07:44.490
No, but...

07:44.490 --> 07:49.980
Come on. If dead pasta started 
moving, it would be zombie pasta!

07:59.260 --> 08:03.860
Does that make this zombie pasta, then?

08:13.420 --> 08:14.800
Ains-san...

08:14.800 --> 08:16.350
Yes, Lady Rem?

08:16.780 --> 08:19.820
Zombies are disgusting, aren't they?

08:20.990 --> 08:23.600
They're undead, like me.

08:25.230 --> 08:27.560
But yeah, I guess they're disgusting.

08:28.710 --> 08:32.150
What is this? What is this? What is this?

08:32.470 --> 08:35.090
Albedo-san, why are you so calm?

08:35.090 --> 08:36.490
They're going to attack!

08:36.490 --> 08:38.250
Don't worry.

08:38.870 --> 08:42.000
Since they're zombies...

08:42.000 --> 08:45.170
The first one of us they'll go for is...

08:51.820 --> 08:53.510
Aqua-san!

08:56.270 --> 08:57.390
Oh, fine.

08:57.660 --> 09:01.610
Neumann! You take care of the one over 
there who they'll probably attack!

09:01.610 --> 09:02.690
On it!

09:03.310 --> 09:06.200
S-Stop!

09:06.200 --> 09:07.840
Miss Lalatina!

09:07.840 --> 09:10.570
Don't call me that!

09:10.570 --> 09:11.300
Let's go, everyone!

09:11.300 --> 09:12.420
OK!

09:12.420 --> 09:13.880
I know that!

09:13.880 --> 09:14.860
Yup!

09:17.100 --> 09:19.620
Wh-What are you doing?

09:18.450 --> 09:24.370
Come on... Why would pasta turn into a 
zombie when you boil it? That's crazy!

09:27.820 --> 09:29.460
Miss Rem, that's...

09:29.460 --> 09:30.740
A cooking utensil.

09:30.740 --> 09:31.740
A cooking utensil?

09:31.740 --> 09:33.210
Yse. A cooking utensil.

10:06.130 --> 10:10.580
I'm having trouble resolving the difference 
between what I'm seeing and what I'm hearing.

10:10.580 --> 10:13.410
You're one to talk, ma'am.

10:13.410 --> 10:15.630
What does that mean?

10:15.860 --> 10:18.450
Weak. Too weak.

10:18.450 --> 10:21.860
Likely because our pasta lacked 
anything to make it special.

10:21.860 --> 10:23.130
Just like Kazuma.

10:23.130 --> 10:26.420
Why do I have to be insulted 
like that over pasta?

10:39.870 --> 10:44.870
Okay, once you throw out the garbage, 
that's it for today's cooking class.

10:45.300 --> 10:47.830
What a mess.

10:47.830 --> 10:49.250
That's right.

10:50.610 --> 10:54.830
Why did the pasta turn into zombies anyway?

10:56.180 --> 10:58.840
Well, let me think...

11:00.870 --> 11:03.450
As expected of a supreme being!

11:06.130 --> 11:10.310
It's just as you were thinking, Ains-sama!

11:12.230 --> 11:14.170
You know the answer, Ains?

11:14.170 --> 11:15.700
Why does he always do this?

11:15.700 --> 11:17.100
You're not getting off me?

11:17.100 --> 11:20.400
It helps with my digestion for some reason.

11:20.400 --> 11:22.680
Rem-san, are you okay?

11:22.680 --> 11:27.450
Yes. I'm not tired, just a little sleepy.

11:27.450 --> 11:29.810
Okay, we're almost done.

11:29.810 --> 11:32.030
Hey, bring that over here, thin-necked man.

11:32.030 --> 11:34.170
You just like saying that.

11:34.170 --> 11:38.260
How long does Wiz-sensei have 
to stay up there, by the way?

11:38.260 --> 11:41.300
Until class is over, I guess.

11:41.300 --> 11:44.170
Then we need to finish the cleaning fast, huh?

11:44.170 --> 11:46.130
That's right, Emilia-tan!

11:48.580 --> 11:50.730
Sneak...

11:51.440 --> 11:52.650
Wait, Visha!

11:52.650 --> 11:55.020
Don't try to eat the corpse of the zombie pasta!
